{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:e32adda02e23d4a6","name":"3Z3 Medical Droid","source":{"id":"source:reference-e32adda02e23d4a6","title":"3Z3 Medical Droid","revision":20108,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T23:13:14Z","sha256":"ba3eed5687030eb057445432717593b2177183f49915619aa4a5aed0d5199693","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20108","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=3Z3%20Medical%20Droid&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-e32adda02e23d4a6","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Legacy Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Legacy_Era_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A cutting-edge replacement for the Medical Droids of the past, the 3Z3 Medical Droid from ",{"tag":"a","children":["Industrial Automaton"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Industrial_Automaton","referenceId":"reference:8ab52c937ff3814a"}," is often touted by its manufacturer as one of the most stable and reliable ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Models"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Models"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The 3Z3 is considered an Imperial Droid, since Imperial interests originally funded the Droid's production. However, the 3Z3 model has been made available for sale to individuals throughout the galaxy. During production, Imperial bureaucrats demanded that ",{"tag":"a","children":["Industrial Automaton"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Industrial_Automaton","referenceId":"reference:8ab52c937ff3814a"}," install combat scenario programming into the Droids, enabling them to replace living combat medics. In battlefield simulations, the 3Z3 Medical Droids perform extremely well, but in the private sector this programming produces somewhat quirky behavior. When put under intense pressure, the 3Z3 Medical Droid's combat scenario programming kicks in, causing the Droid to behave in much the same way it would on the battlefield, rushing from patient to patient and putting patients through a \"triage\" routine that is unnecessary.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Imperial Army makes extensive use of 3Z3 Medical Droids. One such Droid, ",{"tag":"a","children":["K2-3Z3"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/K2-3Z3?action=edit&redlink=1"},", saw to the medical treatment of Sergeant ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ran Harkas"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ran_Harkas?action=edit&redlink=1"}," of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Joker Squad"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Joker_Squad","referenceId":"reference:fdb781529688c891"}," after a skirmish against Fel loyalists on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Borosk"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Borosk?action=edit&redlink=1"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["3Z3 Medical Droids can be played as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Heroes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Heroes"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["3Z3 Medical Droid Statistics (CL 1)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["1st-Degree Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/1st-Degree_Droid"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 4\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +3; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Low-Light Vision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Low-Light_Vision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +11\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Binary"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binary","referenceId":"reference:ee1c8277ca